---
title: Proposition 40
---
order: 40
---
short_label: X.40
---
statement: If two straight lines incommensurable in square which make the sum of the squares on them medial but the rectangle contained by them rational are added together, then the whole straight line is irrational; let it be called the <i>side of a rational plus a medial area.</i>
